From f064faf98d91fb9874198fe50f5aefe41d6517b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ognian Mitzev <OgiMitzev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 00:43:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.55: MSVC ABI flavor in rustc_abi_cxx + target routing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Vendors the v1.09.0 MSVC support from rustcc's workspace
crates/rustc_abi_cxx/ into the in-tree compiler/rustc_abi_cxx/.
This is the foundational patch for the v1.09.1 MSVC C++ ABI
series; subsequent patches consume the AbiFlavor dispatch added
here.

Changes:
- New `AbiFlavor::{Itanium, Msvc}` field on `Target`. Existing
  constructors default to `Itanium` so non-Windows targets see no
  behavior change.
- 3 new Target constructors: `x86_64_pc_windows_msvc`,
  `aarch64_pc_windows_msvc`, `x86_64_pc_windows_gnu` (mingw,
  Itanium-flavored).
- `from_rustc_triple` extended to route Windows triples through
  the new constructors. Unknown triples still fall through to the
  generic Itanium profile.
- New `mangle_msvc`, `layout_msvc`, `vtable_msvc` modules
  implementing the MSVC C++ ABI per the workspace's 65 cross-
  validated golden cases. See the workspace README at
  https://github.com/mitzev/rustcc for the corpus details.
- `mangle()` / `layout()` / `vtable()` on `CxxTypeCtx` become
  dispatchers that route on `target().abi_flavor`. The existing
  Itanium implementations are now `_itanium`-suffixed and still
  exposed for cross-ABI consumers + tests.

All 309 workspace tests pass against the same source under both
paths. The in-tree `rustc_abi_cxx` crate has no consumers in this
patch — the symbol-mangling and layout-bridge call sites that
build a `CxxTypeCtx` already route through the dispatcher
automatically (they call the unchanged `mangle()` / `layout()`
methods that now dispatch internally).
